{"id":"mahabharata-4-017","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":17,"title":"सप्तदशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 17 · Draupadi's lament: Yudhishthira's fall","summary":{"en":"Draupadi laments that a woman whose husband is Yudhishthira must suffer every sorrow. She contrasts his former glory, attended by thousands of elephants and Brahmins, with his present state as a gambler serving another king.","kn":"ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಂಥ ಪತಿಯಿರುವ ಸ್ತ್ರೀ ಎಲ್ಲ ದುಃಖಗಳನ್ನೂ ಅನುಭವಿಸಬೇಕಾಗಿದೆ ಎಂದು ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ವಿಲಪಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಸಾವಿರಾರು ಆನೆ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರಿಂದ ಸೇವಿತನಾಗಿದ್ದ ಅವನ ಹಿಂದಿನ ವೈಭವವನ್ನು ಬೇರೆ ರಾಜನ ಸೇವೆ ಮಾಡುವ ದ್ಯೂತಕಾರನಾದ ಈಗಿನ ಸ್ಥಿತಿಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೋಲಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"द्रौपदी विलाप करती हैं कि जिस स्त्री के पति युधिष्ठिर हों उसे हर दुःख सहना पड़ता है। वे हज़ारों हाथियों और ब्राह्मणों से घिरे उनके पूर्व वैभव की तुलना दूसरे राजा की सेवा करते जुआरी के रूप में उनकी वर्तमान दशा से करती हैं।","te":"యుధిష్ఠిరుని వంటి భర్త ఉన్న స్త్రీ ప్రతి దుఃఖాన్నీ అనుభవించవలసి వస్తోందని ద్రౌపది విలపిస్తుంది. వేలాది ఏనుగులు, బ్రాహ్మణులు సేవించిన అతని పూర్వ వైభవాన్ని మరొక రాజుకు సేవ చేసే జూదరిగా ఇప్పటి స్థితితో పోలుస్తుంది.","ta":"யுதிஷ்டிரரைக் கணவனாகக் கொண்ட பெண் எல்லாத் துயரங்களையும் அனுபவிக்க வேண்டியிருக்கிறது என்று திரௌபதி புலம்புகிறாள். ஆயிரக்கணக்கான யானைகளும் அந்தணர்களும் சூழ்ந்திருந்த அவருடைய முந்தைய பெருமையை, வேறொரு மன்னனுக்குப் பணிபுரியும் சூதாடியான இன்றைய நிலையுடன் ஒப்பிடுகிறாள்.","ml":"യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ ഭർത്താവായുള്ള സ്ത്രീക്ക് എല്ലാ ദുഃഖവും സഹിക്കേണ്ടിവരുന്നുവെന്ന് ദ്രൗപദി വിലപിക്കുന്നു. ആയിരക്കണക്കിന് ആനകളും ബ്രാഹ്മണരും സേവിച്ചിരുന്ന അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ പഴയ മഹത്വത്തെയും, മറ്റൊരു രാജാവിനെ സേവിക്കുന്ന ചൂതുകളിക്കാരനായ ഇപ്പോഴത്തെ അവസ്ഥയെയും അവൾ താരതമ്യം ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.17; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"कीचकवधपर्व","titleEn":"Kichakavadha Parva (Slaying of Kichaka)","verses":[{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अशोच्यं नु कुतस्तस्या यस्या भर्ता युधिष्ठिरः ।\nजानन्सर्वाणि दुःखानि किं मां त्वं परिपृच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"How can she who has Yudhishthira for husband not be pitied? You know all my sorrows; why do you ask me?"}},{"n":2,"text":"यन्मां दासीप्रवादेन प्रातिकामी तदानयत् ।\nसभायां पार्षदो मध्ये तन्मां दहति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"That the Pratikamin dragged me into the court, in the midst of the courtiers, calling me a slave, burns me still, Bharata."}},{"n":3,"text":"पार्थिवस्य सुता नाम का नु जीवेत मादृशी ।\nअनुभूय भृशं दुःखमन्यत्र द्रौपदीं प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"What daughter of a king, apart from Draupadi, having suffered such grief, could live on, lord?"}},{"n":4,"text":"वनवासगतायाश्च सैन्धवेन दुरात्मना ।\nपरामर्शं द्वितीयं च सोढुमुत्सहते नु का ॥","meaning":{"en":"And who could endure being touched again by the wicked king of Sindhu while living in the forest?"}},{"n":5,"text":"मत्स्यराज्ञः समक्षं च तस्य धूर्तस्य पश्यतः ।\nकीचकेन पदा स्पृष्टा का नु जीवेत मादृशी ॥","meaning":{"en":"And being kicked by Kichaka in the presence of the Matsya king, while that cheat looked on: what woman like me could live?"}},{"n":6,"text":"एवं बहुविधैः क्लेशैः क्लिश्यमानां च भारत ।\nन मां जानासि कौन्तेय किं फलं जीवितेन मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, you do not know me, tormented by so many kinds of suffering, son of Kunti; what use is life to me?"}},{"n":7,"text":"योऽयं राज्ञो विराटस्य कीचको नाम भारत ।\nसेनानीः पुरुषव्याघ्र स्यालः परमदुर्मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This Kichaka, King Virata's brother-in-law and army-leader, tiger among men, is exceedingly wicked."}},{"n":8,"text":"स मां सैरन्ध्रिवेषेण वसन्तीं राजवेश्मनि ।\nनित्यमेवाह दुष्टात्मा भार्या मम भवेति वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I live in the king's house disguised as a sairandhri, that evil-minded man says to me every day, \"Be my wife.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"तेनोपमन्त्र्यमाणाया वधार्हेण सपत्नहन् ।\nकालेनेव फलं पक्वं हृदयं मे विदीर्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Slayer of foes, while that man who deserves death solicits me, my heart is splitting like a fruit ripened by time."}},{"n":10,"text":"भ्रातरं च विगर्हस्व ज्येष्ठं दुर्द्यूतदेविनम् ।\nयस्यास्मि कर्मणा प्राप्ता दुःखमेतदनन्तकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Blame your eldest brother, the gambler at evil dice, by whose act I have come to this endless sorrow."}},{"n":11,"text":"को हि राज्यं परित्यज्य सर्वस्वं चात्मना सह ।\nप्रव्रज्यायैव दीव्येत विना दुर्द्यूतदेविनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For who except one addicted to evil dice would give up his kingdom and all his wealth, and gamble just to go into exile?"}},{"n":12,"text":"यदि निष्कसहस्रेण यच्चान्यत्सारवद्धनम् ।\nसायंप्रातरदेविष्यदपि संवत्सरान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If he had played morning and evening for many years with a thousand gold nishkas and every other treasure,"}},{"n":13,"text":"रुक्मं हिरण्यं वासांसि यानं युग्यमजाविकम् ।\nअश्वाश्वतरसंघांश्च न जातु क्षयमावहेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"he would never have exhausted his gold, silver, garments, carriages, teams, goats and sheep, horses and mule-herds."}},{"n":14,"text":"सोऽयं द्यूतप्रवादेन श्रिया प्रत्यवरोपितः ।\nतूष्णीमास्ते यथा मूढः स्वानि कर्माणि चिन्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet by the pretext of dice he was cast down from his fortune, and now he sits silent like a fool, brooding over his own deeds."}},{"n":15,"text":"दश नागसहस्राणि पद्मिनां हेममालिनाम् ।\nयं यान्तमनुयान्तीह सोऽयं द्यूतेन जीवति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whom ten thousand elephants with golden garlands and lotus decorations followed when he traveled lives now by dice."}},{"n":16,"text":"तथा शतसहस्राणि नृणाममिततेजसाम् ।\nउपासते महाराजमिन्द्रप्रस्थे युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hundreds of thousands of men of boundless power served the great king Yudhishthira at Indraprastha."}},{"n":17,"text":"शतं दासीसहस्राणि यस्य नित्यं महानसे ।\nपात्रीहस्तं दिवारात्रमतिथीन्भोजयन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In whose great kitchen a hundred thousand maidservants, plate in hand, fed guests day and night."}},{"n":18,"text":"एष निष्कसहस्राणि प्रदाय ददतां वरः ।\nद्यूतजेन ह्यनर्थेन महता समुपावृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This best of givers, who gave away thousands of nishkas, is now engulfed in great misfortune born of dice."}},{"n":19,"text":"एनं हि स्वरसंपन्ना बहवः सूतमागधाः ।\nसायंप्रातरुपातिष्ठन्सुमृष्टमणिकुण्डलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many sweet-voiced bards and chroniclers, with polished jeweled earrings, served him morning and evening."}},{"n":20,"text":"सहस्रमृषयो यस्य नित्यमासन्सभासदः ।\nतपःश्रुतोपसंपन्नाः सर्वकामैरुपस्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A thousand sages with austerity and learning always sat in his assembly and were supplied with all they desired."}},{"n":21,"text":"अन्धान्वृद्धांस्तथानाथान्सर्वान्राष्ट्रेषु दुर्गतान् ।\nबिभर्त्यविमना नित्यमानृशंस्याद्युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, out of constant compassion, cheerfully supported all the blind, the aged and the helpless, and all the destitute in his realm."}},{"n":22,"text":"स एष निरयं प्राप्तो मत्स्यस्य परिचारकः ।\nसभायां देविता राज्ञः कङ्को ब्रूते युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That same man has come to hell, a servant of the Matsya king, a dice-player in the court who says he is Kanka, though he is Yudhishthira."}},{"n":23,"text":"इन्द्रप्रस्थे निवसतः समये यस्य पार्थिवाः ।\nआसन्बलिभृतः सर्वे सोऽद्यान्यैर्भृतिमिच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He at whose court at Indraprastha all kings paid tribute now seeks wages from others."}},{"n":24,"text":"पार्थिवाः पृथिवीपाला यस्यासन्वशवर्तिनः ।\nस वशे विवशो राजा परेषामद्य वर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kings and protectors of the earth who were once subject to him, that same king is now helplessly in others' power."}},{"n":25,"text":"प्रताप्य पृथिवीं सर्वां रश्मिवानिव तेजसा ।\nसोऽयं राज्ञो विराटस्य सभास्तारो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having scorched the whole earth with his might like the sun with its rays, he is now King Virata's courtier, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":26,"text":"यमुपासन्त राजानः सभायामृषिभिः सह ।\nतमुपासीनमद्यान्यं पश्य पाण्डव पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See, Pandava, the one whom kings with sages attended in the assembly, now attending another man, he a Pandava."}},{"n":27,"text":"अतदर्हं महाप्राज्ञं जीवितार्थेऽभिसंश्रितम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा कस्य न दुःखं स्याद्धर्मात्मानं युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the wise, righteous Yudhishthira, unfit for it, dependent on others for his living, whose heart would not grieve?"}},{"n":28,"text":"उपास्ते स्म सभायां यं कृत्स्ना वीर वसुंधरा ।\nतमुपासीनमद्यान्यं पश्य भारत भारतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See, Bharata, the one whom the whole earth attended in the assembly, now attending another, he the best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":29,"text":"एवं बहुविधैर्दुःखैः पीड्यमानामनाथवत् ।\nशोकसागरमध्यस्थां किं मां भीम न पश्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, afflicted by such manifold sorrows like one without protectors, immersed in a sea of grief, why do you not see me?"}}]}]}